{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}],"title":"MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MaximalCliques.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques.swift#L259"},"externalID":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/makeIterator()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generate